      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">Maltose is composed of two glucose molecules linked by an &amp;alpha; 1,4-glycosidic linkage. Maltose is produced by the hydrolysis of starch and similar compounds, and can be hydrolyzed to glucose by the enzyme maltase.</Comment>
