      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">This class of compounds represents a set of unbranched linear chains of glucose residues linked to each other in an &amp;alpha;(1-&gt;4) configuration. In the structure shown, the R group would be one or more additional units of glucose |CITS: [20192737]|. The naming of various instances of this class of compounds is based on the number of glucosyl residues in the chain. For example, maltotetraose has 4 glucose subunits |CITS: [20192737]|.</Comment>
